     I haven't read the relevant section of the wiki, but it
sounds like someone has oversimplified to the point of being
wrong.  Nearly any spell casting monster (aside from priests,
who use a different set of spells) can cast Touch of Death if
its level is high enough.  A kobold shaman can do so, given
enough potions of gain level.

     The default level for master liches is 17, which is too
low to cast that spell (minimum level needed is 21).  But 17
is just a starting point; they can be created with level
anywhere from 16 to 25, depending upon depth of the dungeon
level and hero's experience level.  [16: 17-1; 25: 3*17/2;
see adj_lev(makemon.c).]  They can also drink potions of gain
level; they won't turn into arch-liches until level 25 (26 if
created at level 25 to begin with).

     So a master lich certainly can cast Touch of Death.  At
level 21, chance per spell cast is about 4.75% [1 out of 21];
at 23, it's 13% [3 out of 23].  Due to a quirk in spell
selection, the chance gradually gets lower as monster level
goes higher than 23 [3 out of <monlvl>].


